    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan calls for maintaining current positioning at ~$177.33 given the balanced technical picture. JPM is a high-quality institution in a short-term pullback within a long-term uptrend, but the technical picture is not yet confirmed as a reversal. The stock remains below the 50-day SMA ($178.86) and VWMA ($180.19), MACD is still negative at -1.60, and RSI is below 50. However, the bull case is supported by improving momentum (RSI recovering from 30.39 to 43.91, three consecutive days of MACD histogram improvement, higher low at $173.14) and a fortress balance sheet with $327.9B in equity. Neither the bullish \"buy the dip\" thesis nor the bearish \"sell/avoid\" thesis is strong enough to justify a decisive move. The prudent action is to hold and wait for confirmation\u2014either a reclaim of the 50 SMA on strong volume (bullish trigger) or a break below $171.46 (bearish trigger).\n\n**Entry Price**: 177.33\n\n**Stop Loss**: 171.46\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain standard allocation; do not add new exposure until 50-day SMA is reclaimed on above-average volume. Keep position size moderate given elevated volatility (ATR of 3.50, realized vol of 27.76%).\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
